ceived) + (consumed) &#x02013; (produced).</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-ijerph-06-00108"><label>c:</label><p>Potential loss = (net investment) + (did not produce) &#x02013; (did not receive) &#x02013; (did not consume). Note: negative investments and negative losses are gains to society. Source: [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b2-ijerph-06-00108">2</xref>], p. 326</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></app></app-group><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="b1-ijerph-06-00108"><label>1.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Centre for Disease Control Premature Mortality in The United States: Public Health Issues in The Use of Years of Potential Life Lost</collab></person-group><source>Morbidity and Mortality Weekly Report</source><volume>35</volume><issue>2S</issue><fpage>1s</fpage><lpage>11s</lpage><publisher-name>Centre for Disease Control and Prevention, US Department of Health and Human Services</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Atlanta, GA, USA</publisher-loc><year>1986</year></citation></ref><ref id="b2-ijerph-06-00108"><label>2.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanborn</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Years of potential life loss (YPLL) - What does it measure?</article-title><source>Epidemiology</source><year>1990</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>322</fpage><lpage>329</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2083312</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b3-ijerph-06-00108"><label>3.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NSW Department of Health Inpatient Statistics Collection (ISC)</collab></person-group><source>Health Outcomes Information and Statistical Tool Kit (HOIST)</source><publisher-name>New South Wales Health</publisher-name><publisher-loc>North Sydney, Australia</publisher-loc><year>2002</year></citation